CB010846_RU_resilency_controlled_case_hard_RAT_reset
    [Documentation]
    ...  Purpose of this test case is to check if RMOD did not reset during “cntrldResetMplaneBreakTime” duration after RAT
    ...  and BBMOD reset.
    ...
    ...  ARGS:
    ...  :param (int or str) rmod_id: (Mandatory) : RMOD configuration id of tested radio module, e.g.: 1
    ...  :param (dict) throughputs: dict with throughput and deviation values for each teste RMOD's cell identified by it's nrCellIdentity.
    ...                             Example:
    ...                               {
    ...                                   '827736065':
    ...                                        {
    ...                                             'throughput':
    ...                                                {
    ...                                                    'downlink': '100 Mbits/sec',
    ...                                                    'uplink': '15 Mbits/sec'
    ...                                                 },
    ...                                            'deviation': '90%'
    ...                                        },
    ...                                }
    ...  :param (str) protocol: data transfer protocol; defaults to UDP.
    ...  :param (str) udp_buffer: monitoring data buffer; defaults to 4M.
    ...  :param (bool) tput_verification_via_btslog: True - throughput verification will be performed using btslog
    ...                                              False - throuput verification will be performed using iperf; defaults to False
    ...  :param (dict) ue_network_modes: dict with UE serial numbers and desired network modes e.g. {"SN1234": "NR_only"}
    ...                                  possible UE network modes: NR_only, LTE_only, NR_LTE
    ...                                  when using more than one UE please make sure that the modes you choose are either all
    ...                                  with "_only" suffix or all "NR_LTE" as it is not yet possible to mix those.
    ...                                  mandatory for SA+NSA setups, defaults to None
    ...  :param (dict) ues_and_cells: dict with UE serial numbers and lists of configuration distnames of cells to which they
    ...                               can be attached e.g. {"SN1234": ["MRBTS-50146/NRBTS-1/NRCELL-1", "MRBTS-50146/NRBTS-1/NRCELL-3"],
    ...                                                     "SN5678": ["MRBTS-50146/NRBTS-1/NRCELL-5"]}
    ...                               defaults to ${None} which means that all UEs will be attached to all cells.
    ...                               when given, listed cells will be called in pairs with specified UEs, if there are more
    ...                               cells on the setup that were not mentioned in the list, they will be called with all UEs

    [Arguments]    ${rmod_id}
    ...            ${throughputs}=${None}
    ...            ${protocol}=udp
    ...            ${udp_buffer}=4M
    ...            ${tput_verification_via_btslog}=${False}
    ...            ${ue_network_modes}=${None}
    ...            ${ues_and_cells}=${None}

    ${bts_type}                                             hwpta_testline.get_type_of_setup
    ${connection}                                           connections.get_default_admin_connection_alias
    ...                                                     bts_type=${bts_type}

    ${all_cells_of_rmod}                                    admin_info_model.get_configuration_distnames_of_all_cells_for_rmod
    ...                                                     rmod_id=${rmod_id}
    ...                                                     connection=${connection}

    ${rmod_startup_before_nr_rat_reset}                     Get DateTime of Last RMOD Startup
    ...                                                     rmod_id=${rmod_id}
    ...                                                     connection=${connection}

    ${env_vrf}                                              Get Library Instance
    ...                                                     rat_env_vrf
    Call method                                             ${env_vrf}
    ...                                                     initialize
    ...                                                     reset_rat=nr
    ...                                                     reset_type=hard
    ...                                                     connection_alias=${connection}

    Hard Reset NR RAT and Wait for Status Change            env_vrf=${env_vrf}
    ...                                                     connection=${connection}

    Check All Components During RAT Reset                   env_vrf=${env_vrf}
    ...                                                     connection=${connection}

    Run keyword if                                          ${throughputs}
    ...                                                     Run keywords
    ...                                                     Robot Log Operation
    ...                                                     Checking L3 call unavailability on cells commissioned on impacted RMOD-${rmod_id}
    ...                                                     AND
    ...                                                     Execute L3 Call Attach Should Not be Possible
    ...                                                     cell_distnames=${all_cells_of_rmod}
    ...                                                     should_fid49_be_disallowed=${True}
    ...                                                     prepare_cells_to_call=${False}
    ...                                                     AND
    ...                                                     Robot Log Operation
    ...                                                     L3 call is unavailable on impacted RMOD-${rmod_id}.

    Check Statuses after NR RAT Reset and Wait for OnAir    bts_type=${bts_type}

    Run keyword if                                          ${throughputs}
    ...                                                     Run keywords
    ...                                                     Robot Log Operation
    ...                                                     Checking L3 call availiability on cells commissioned on impacted RMOD-${rmod_id}
    ...                                                     AND
    ...                                                     Execute L3 call
    ...                                                     cells_distnames=${all_cells_of_rmod}
    ...                                                     throughputs=${throughputs}
    ...                                                     protocol=${protocol}
    ...                                                     udp_buffer=${udp_buffer}
    ...                                                     tput_verification_via_btslog=${tput_verification_via_btslog}
    ...                                                     ue_network_modes=${ue_network_modes}
    ...                                                     ues_and_cells=${ues_and_cells}
    ...                                                     AND
    ...                                                     Robot Log Operation
    ...                                                     L3 call is available on impacted RMOD-${rmod_id}.

    ${rmod_startup_after_nr_rat_reset}                      Get DateTime of Last RMOD Startup
    ...                                                     rmod_id=${rmod_id}
    ...                                                     connection=${connection}

    Robot Log Operation                                     Verifying if RMOD-${rmod_id} has been reset during NR RAT reset...
    Verify If RMOD Has Been Reset                           reference_startup_datetime=${rmod_startup_before_nr_rat_reset}
    ...                                                     actual_startup_datetime=${rmod_startup_after_nr_rat_reset}
    ...                                                     expect_rmod_reset=${False}
    Robot Log Result                                        RMOD-${rmod_id} has not been reset during NR RAT reset.

    [Teardown]                                              RU Resilency Hard RAT Reset Teardown
    ...                                                     bts_type=${bts_type}

Hard Reset NR RAT and Wait for Status Change
    [Arguments]    ${env_vrf}
    ...            ${connection}

    Robot Log Operation                                     Performing reset NR RAT...
    Alarms.Allow X2 Link Alarms

    admin_info_model.reset_rat_in_separate_process          rat=nr
    ...                                                     reset_type=hard

    wait until keyword succeeds                             3m
    ...                                                     5s
    ...                                                     status_check.verify_statuses_of_rats
    ...                                                     rats=${env_vrf.get_affected_rat_with_variant()}
    ...                                                     connection=${connection}

    Robot Log Operation                                     NR RAT Reset has been performed.

